# Cloudflare Pages headers file.
#
# Inactive today: the live site is served by GitHub Pages, which cannot read
# this file at all (and Jekyll excludes underscore-prefixed files from its
# output anyway). It takes effect the moment Cloudflare Pages serves the site.
#
# Deliberately conservative — nothing here changes what a visitor sees or how
# the pages behave. No CSP yet: the site loads GA4 and the Cloudflare Analytics
# beacon from third-party origins, so a CSP needs its own change with its own
# verification pass, not a line smuggled into a hosting migration.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
